              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new word: what did chatram mean?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: कदाचित्",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "कदाचित् (kadācit) — \"sometimes\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "कदाचित् (kadācit) answers \"when?\" with \"now and then\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Both pieces are yours already: कदा, the when you ask questions with, and a small cit fastened on the end. कदाचित् (kadācit) is when gone vague — at some time or other, and no promise which."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "It is also the polite way to leave a door open: not yes, not no, perhaps sometimes."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "A reply that answers when without saying when."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 1,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 1s]"
            },
            {
